{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Integrate the EASS into the EHRC and restore EHRC statutory duties",
        "additional_details": "In 2010 the EHRC\u2019s helpline and conciliation services were removed. Reports indicate that this, along with cuts to legal aid, resulted in a 50% reduction in the number of disability discrimination claims.\r\n \r\nIn 2016 the House of Lords Select Committee on the Equality Act 2010 and Disability called for:\r\n \r\n1. return of the EASS helpline to the EHRC\r\n2. restoration of conciliation and direct legal advice.\r\n3. integration of helpline data into strategic enforcement.\r\n4.development of in-person and accessible legal support.\r\n \r\nWe feel these changes are long overdue.",
        "background": "My petition calls on the Government to:\r\n- Integrate the Equality Advisory and Support Service (EASS) into the EHRC.\r\n- Restore the EHRC\u2019s statutory duty to provide legal advice, conciliation, and strategic casework.\r\n",
